      title: 'Durak Severnyi (Northern Durak)',
      subtitle: 'Shedding rules and play flow',
    },
    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Durak Severnyi (Northern Durak)',
            subtitle: 'Shedding rules and play flow',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Durak Severnyi (Northern Fool) is an atmospheric and high-stakes variant of the Russian card game Durak, primarily played in the Northern regions of Russia and Siberia. While it follows the standard Podkidnoy (throw-in) mechanics for the majority of the game, it contains a legendary 'sting in the tail': a late-game trump suit shift. By hiding the final trump identity until the very last card is drawn, Durak Severnyi forces players to maintain a balanced hand of all suits, as a dominant lead in the initial trump suit can instantly turn into a liability at the game's climax.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Originating in the Arkhangelsk and Vologda regions, this variant reflected the unpredictable and harsh nature of the Northern Russian climate. It was designed to prevent 'trump hoarding'â€”a common strategy in standard Durak that can make the endgame predictable.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '2-6 players. Best with 3-4 to ensure the Secret Trump phase is reached.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '36-card Russian pack (6, 7, 8, 9, 10, J, Q, K, A).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '36-card deck.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '1. Each player is dealt 6 cards.\n2. One card is placed FACE-DOWN in the center.\n3. The next card is placed FACE-UP on top of it (The Initial Trump Suit).\n4. The stock is placed on top of these two cards.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: "Secret Trump (Trump Shift): After the face-up trump is drawn as second-to-last from the stock, the player who draws the final face-down card reveals it; that card's suit becomes the new trump for the rest of the game; the former trump becomes an ordinary suit. If the face-down card is the same suit as the initial trump, nothing changes.",
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Other: No further documented variants in primary sources.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Reserved: No further documented variants in primary sources.',
                  },
                ],
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
    description: "Durak Severnyi (Northern Fool) is an atmospheric and high-stakes variant of the Russian card game Durak, primarily played in the Northern regions of Russia and Siberia. While it follows the standard Podkidnoy (throw-in) mechanics for the majority of the game, it contains a legendary 'sting in the tail': a late-game trump suit shift. By hiding the final trump identity until the very last card is drawn, Durak Severnyi forces players to maintain a balanced hand of all suits, as a dominant lead in the initial trump suit can instantly turn into a liability at the game's climax.",
