          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: "Escape the 'Fool' (Durak) title by shedding all cards, especially during the chaotic trump-shift endgame.",
          gameplay: '1. Standard Play: Follow Podkidnoy rules (Attacking, Defending, Throw-ins).\n2. Initial Trump: Use the face-up card suit for the first phase.\n3. The Shift: When the stock is empty, the player who draws the LAST (face-down) card reveals it.\n4. New Reality: The suit of that final card IMMEDIATELY becomes the new trump suit for the rest of the game.',
          keyRules: [
            'The change of trump suit happens instantly; currently active attacks are resolved using the NEW suit.',
            "If the face-down card matches the initial trump suit, nothing changes (a 'lucky North').",
            'Standard attack limits (6 cards) apply.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Do not burn all your non-trump high cards (Aces/Kings) early. In Severnyi, those 'junk' cards might become trumps in the final five minutes of the game.",
          intermediate: 'Hand Diversification: Unlike standard Durak where you want to empty yourself of non-trump suits, in Severnyi, you should try to keep at least one high card of every suit until the final card is revealed.',
          advanced: "Counting the Talon: Track how many cards are left in the stock. If you are the one about to draw the final card, try to ensure you have a hand that benefits from a 'random' suit becoming trumps.",
          tips: [
            'Revealing the final card is a massive tactical moment. If you are the one revealed it, you have the first knowledge of the new landscapeâ€”use it to attack effectively.',
            "If you held the 6 of the initial trump suit (allowing you to exchange for the face-up card), do so early; it won't be worth much if the suit changes.",
          ],
