        synthesis: {
          hero: {
            title: 'Durak Severnyi (Northern Durak)',
            subtitle: 'Shedding rules and play flow',
            tagline: 'Durak Severnyi (Northern Fool) is an atmospheric and high-stakes variant of the Russian card game Durak, primarily played in the Northern regions of Russia and Siberia.',
          },
          shortDescription: "Durak Severnyi (Northern Fool) is an atmospheric and high-stakes variant of the Russian card game Durak, primarily played in the Northern regions of Russia and Siberia. While it follows the standard Podkidnoy (throw-in) mechanics for the majority of the game, it contains a legendary 'sting in the tail': a late-game trump suit shift. By hiding the final trump identity until the very last card is drawn, Durak Severnyi forces players to maintain a balanced hand of all suits, as a dominant lead in the initial trump suit can instantly turn into a liability at the game's climax.",
